(30243,0,3,'I will take pleasure in gutting you!',12,0,100,0,0,14384,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,4,'Sniveling pig!',12,0,100,0,0,14394,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,5,'Ugglin oo bjorr!',12,0,100,0,0,14395,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,6,'You come to die!',12,0,100,0,0,14392,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,7,'Die, maggot!',12,0,100,0,0,14391,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,8,'Haraak foln!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,9,'Your entrails will make a fine necklace.',12,0,100,0,0,14386,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,10,'Die, maggot!',12,0,100,0,0,14387,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30243,0,11,'Your entrails will make a fine necklace.',12,0,100,0,0,14390,'Njorndar Spear-Sister'),
(30292,0,0,'This bear\'s flank is frozen solid.... try again.',42,0,0,0,0,0,''),
(30381,0,0,'And it very nearly didn\'t remember you. $n fought bravely against the North Wind to protect your story.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,1,0,'Your battle with the wind was hundreds of years ago, Stormhoof. You weakened it so much that it has been silent all these years.',12,0,100,273,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,2,0,'But the North Wind did not silently accept defeat. Instead, it gathered power and bided its time, deciding the best revenge was to destroy your memory, and with it, your village.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,3,0,'The wind used its minions to distort the history of this place, changing the stories your people told, destroying the spirits of the honored dead.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,4,0,'It would\'ve succeeded if $n and I hadn\'t tracked the North Wind\'s historical corruptions to their source: your ancient battle.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,5,0,'With my help, $n travelled back in time to your battle, and ensured that history was set right. The North Wind\'s fate was sealed, and your story restored.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,6,0,'Rest well, hero.',12,0,100,273,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,7,0,'This isn\'t right at all, $n. In the tale Wind Tamer Barah told me, Stormhoof was a hero, not a villain.',12,0,100,6,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,8,0,'The North Wind is the ancient enemy of the taunka, a ruler among the elements, and the very force which bleeds the life from these ancient people.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,9,0,'They would rather die than bow before the North Wind. Something is amiss here.',12,0,100,274,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,10,0,'The Lorehammer...',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,11,0,'It confirms our suspicions. The threads of time have been severed and rewoven in the wrong pattern. But, how?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,12,0,'There\'s no doubt that something has distorted the true history of Stormhoof and the warriors of Camp Tunka\'lo. But, what?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,13,0,'No! The true voice of history will triumph. We will restore all you have destroyed!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30381,14,0,'$n, we must hurry and discover when the North Wind has started distorting the timeline. Only then can we defeat him and correct it.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Xarantaur'),
(30390,0,0,'King Jokkum, you have summoned me?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Thorim  - Conversation 18 sec in'),
(30390,1,0,'Jokkum, son of Arngrim, I have always regretted my actions here. In my grief, I brought great harm to those closest to me.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Thorim  - Conversation 26 sec in'),
(30390,2,0,'I would ask your forgiveness for the suffering I have caused you and your people.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Thorim - Conversation 32 sec in'),
(30390,3,0,'Krolmir... I thank you Jokkum. I hadn\'t dared hope it still existed. It shall soon see glorious battle once again!',12,0,100,396,0,0,'Thorim - Conversation 68 sec in'),
(30474,0,0,'Fool! You will never defeat me!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'North Wind'),
(30474,1,0,'I will never allow you to use the Horn of Elemental Fury against us! Die, weakling!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'North Wind'),
(30632,0,0,'Your entrails will make a fine necklace.',12,0,100,0,0,13535,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30632,0,1,'I\'ll eat your heart!',12,0,100,0,0,13695,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30632,0,2,'Haraak foln!',12,0,100,0,0,13541,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30632,0,3,'I\'ll eat your heart!',12,0,100,0,0,13542,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30632,0,4,'Sniveling pig!',12,0,100,0,0,13539,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30632,0,5,'I spit on you!',12,0,100,0,0,13538,'Mjordin Water Magus'),
(30656,0,0,'Hail. I could not help but overhear your conversation. Please allow me to lend some assistance.',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(30725,0,0,'You come to die!',12,0,100,0,0,13537,'Jotunheim Sleep-Watcher'),
(30725,0,1,'I spit on you!',12,0,100,0,0,13537,'Jotunheim Sleep-Watcher'),
(30725,0,2,'Your entrails will make a fine necklace.',12,0,100,0,0,13535,'Jotunheim Sleep-Watcher'),
(30956,0,0,'I knew that you would come.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(30956,1,0,'You have some fight in you. I\'m impressed.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(30956,2,0,'Welcome to the world of the unliving.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(30956,3,0,'Well fought...',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(31135,0,0,'Valhalas is yours to win or die in, $n. But whatever you do, stay within the bounds of the arena. To flee is to lose and be dishonored.',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 1 say 1'),
(31135,1,1,'$n and $g his : her; comrades in arms have chosen to accept honorable combat within the sacred confines of Valhalas.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 1 say 2'),
(31135,2,2,'There can be only one outcome to such a battle: death for one side or the other. Let $n prove $g himself : herself; upon the bones of those outsiders who have fallen before!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 1 say 3'),
(31135,3,3,'The fallen heroes of Valhalas emerge from the ground to do battle once more!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 1 say 4'),
(31135,4,4,'$n has defeated the fallen heroes of Valhalas battles past. This is only a beginning, but it will suffice.',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 1 say 5'),
(31135,5,5,'Prepare yourself. Khit\'rix will be entering Valhalas from the southeast. Remember, do not leave the ring or you will lose the battle.',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 2 say 1'),
(31135,6,6,'$n has accepted the challenge of Khit\'rix the Dark Master. May the gods show mercy upon $g him : her; for Khit\'rix surely will not.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 2 say 2'),
(31135,7,7,'Khit\'rix the Dark Master skitters into Valhalas from the southeast!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 2 say 3'),
(31135,8,8,'Khit\'rix the Dark Master has been defeated by $n and $g his : her; band of companions. Let the next challenge be issued!',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 2 sasy 4'),
(31135,9,9,'Sigrid Iceborn has returned to the heights of Jotunheim to prove herself against $n.  When last they met, $n bested her in personal combat.  Let us see the outcome of this match.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 3 say 1'),
(31135,10,10,'Circling Valhalas, Sigrid Iceborn approaches to seek her revenge!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 3 say 2'),
(31135,11,11,'$n has defeated Sigrid Iceborn for a second time.  Well, this time $g he : she; did it with the help of $g his : her; friends, but a win is a win!',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 3 say 3'),
(31135,12,12,'Carnage is coming!  Remember, no matter what you do, do NOT leave the battle ring or I will disqualify you and your group.',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 4 say 1'),
(31135,13,13,'From the bowels of the Underhalls comes Carnage.  Brave and foolish $n has accepted the challenge.  $G He : She; and $g his : her; group stand ready to face the monstrosity.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 4 say 2'),
(31135,14,14,'Lumbering in from the south, the smell of Carnage precedes him!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 4 say 3'),
(31135,15,15,'The horror known as Carnage is no more.  Could it be that $n is truly worthy of battle in Valhalas?  We shall see.',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 4 say 4'),
(31135,16,16,'Look to the southeast and you will see the thane upon the platform near Gjonner the Merciless when he shows himself. Let him come down.  Stay within the ring of Valhalas.',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 5 say 1'),
(31135,17,17,'Thane Banahogg returns to Valhalas for the first time in ages to prove that the vrykul are the only beings worthy to fight within its sacred ring.  Will $n prove him wrong?',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 5 say 2'),
(31135,18,18,'Thane Banahogg appears upon the overlook to the southeast!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 5 say 3');
INSERT INTO `tmp_548_creature_text` (`entry`,`groupid`,`id`,`text`,`type`,`language`,`probability`,`emote`,`duration`,`sound`,`comment`) VALUES
(31135,19,19,'Thane Banahogg the Deathblow has fallen to $n and $g his : her; fighting companions.  $G He : She; has but one challenge ahead of $g him : her;.  Who will it be?',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 5 say 4'),
(31135,20,20,'It\'s too late to run now.  Do not leave the ring.  Die bravely, $n!',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 6 say 1'),
(31135,21,21,'From the depths of Icecrown Citadel, one of the Lich King\'s chosen comes to put an end to the existence of $n and $g his : her; friends.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 6 say 2'),
(31135,22,22,'Warriors of Jotunheim, I present to you, Blood Prince Sandoval!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 6 say 3'),
(31135,23,23,'Without warning, Prince Sandoval magically appears within Valhalas!',41,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 6 say 4'),
(31135,24,24,'The unthinkable has happened... $n has slain Prince Sandoval!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 6 say 5'),
(31135,25,25,'In defeating him, $g he : she; and $g his : her; fighting companions have proven themselves worthy of battle in this most sacred place of vrykul honor.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff quest 6 say 6'),
(31135,26,26,'ALL HAIL $n, CHAMPION OF VALHALAS!',14,0,0,0,0,14998,'Greiff quest 6 say 7'),
(31135,27,27,'You were not prepared!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Greiff kill'),
(31161,0,0,'I knew that you would come.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(31161,1,0,'You have some fight in you. I\'m impressed.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(31161,2,0,'Welcome to the world of the unliving.',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(31161,3,0,'Well fought...',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Sapph'),
(31222,0,0,'When I am done here, I am going to mount your heads upon the walls of Azjol-Nerub!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Dark Master say 1'),
(31235,0,0,'Thank the Light for granting me another chance. And thank you, $n.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Crusader Olakin Sainrith'),
(31235,1,0,'Without your help, I would\'ve been doomed to a life of undeath among the Lich King\'s gruesome creations.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Crusader Olakin Sainrith'),
(31235,2,0,'There will be time for a proper thanks later, but there is still a battle to be fought!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Crusader Olakin Sainrith'),
(31242,0,0,'Ah, there you are! Remember me? Of course you do! Wait right there, I\'m coming down.',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Sigrid Iceborn say 1'),
(31242,1,0,'I told you I\'d be better prepared when next we met. I\'ve fought and won the Hyldsmeet, trained at Valkyrion, and here I am.  Come and get some!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Sigrid Iceborn say 2'),
(31258,0,0,'I will take pleasure in gutting you!',12,0,100,0,0,13533,'Ymirheim Chosen Warrior'),
(31258,0,1,'I\'ll eat your heart!',12,0,100,1,0,13542,'Ymirheim Chosen Warrior'),
(31277,0,0,'ENOUGH!  You tiny insects are not worthy to do battle within this sacred place!  You do not fight with honor!  You do not even ascend! ',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Thane say 1'),
(31277,1,0,'Fight me and die you cowards!',14,0,0,0,0,0,'Thane say 2'),
(31277,2,0,'Haraak foln!',12,0,0,0,0,0,'Thane say 3'),
(31279,0,0,'Face your judgment by the Light!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31279,0,1,'You will never take me alive!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31279,1,0,'The Light\'s blessing be upon you for aiding me in my time of need, $n.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31279,2,0,'I\'ve had my fill of this place. Let us depart.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31279,3,0,'You must tell my brothers that I live.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31279,4,0,'I have you to thank for my life. I will return to my comrades and spread word of your bravery. Fight the Scourge with all the strength you can muster, and we will be by your side.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Father Kamaros'),
(31306,0,0,'Knights of the Ebon Blade, prepare for battle!',12,0,100,1,0,0,'DHAKAR SAY 1'),
(31428,0,0,'You will pay for what you\'ve done! For the Argent Crusade!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'OLAKIN SAY 1'),
(31810,0,0,'Right. Let\'s see if we can finish this keystone.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Brann Bronzebeard'),
(31810,1,0,'The keystone is completed! We\'ve done it, $n!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Brann Bronzebeard'),
(31810,2,0,'Who knows what secrets await within Ulduar\'s archives? I\'m off to discover them. Thank you again for your help, $n. Without it, I\'d still be searching for that key.',12,0,100,66,0,0,'Brann Bronzebeard'),
(32149,0,0,'It was awful... I dreamt I was fighting against my friends.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Fallen Hero\'s Spirit'),
(32149,0,1,'I\'m so tired. Just let me rest for a moment.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Fallen Hero\'s Spirit'),
(32149,0,2,'I can\'t hear the screams anymore. Is this the end?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Fallen Hero\'s Spirit'),
(32149,0,3,'At last... now I can rest.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Fallen Hero\'s Spirit'),
(32149,0,4,'My nightmare, is it finally over?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Fallen Hero\'s Spirit'),
(32236,0,0,'I feel funny all of a sudden.  Er?!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(32236,0,1,'Okay, who\'s the joker that threw an orb at me?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(32236,0,2,'What?!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(32236,1,0,'It was an accident. I was framed. Don\'t drop me!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(32236,1,1,'You\'ve got it all wrong. I\'m a subjugator!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(32236,1,2,'NOOOOOO!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Dark Subjugator'),
(33027,0,0,'Let me know if you need help finding anything, $c.',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Jessica Sellers'),
(33027,0,1,'Greetings, $c.',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Jessica Sellers'),
(33027,0,2,'Welcome. May I help you find something?',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Jessica Sellers'),
(33027,0,3,'Greetings! Please have a look around.',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Jessica Sellers'),
(33027,0,4,'Welcome.',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Jessica Sellers'),
